From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 16:58:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01830/11362] [conductor] Pre-gate block: PHASE A3 (THE
 HEADLINE GATE, gated_on A2 selector_trained) -- does the ORACLE-DISTINCT
 learned ARC verifier BEAT majority vote OFF-ORACLE? On a HELD-OUT ARC
 candidate pool, rerank with the A2 learned verifier
 (verifier_is_oracle=false; does NOT execute the demos) vs majority-vote vs a
 MATCHED no-verifier control (same candidates/budget) vs oracle@K (the
 positive-control ceiling). The LOAD-BEARING gate: verifier@1 - vote@1,
 bootstrap CI95 EXCLUDES 0 AND headroom exists (oracle@K >> vote). Framed by
 ARBITER (arXiv:2605.26172) 'wrong-majority failures' -- the correct answer is
 in the pool but loses to a bigger wrong basin; the oracle-distinct verifier's
 job is to recover it. YES -> the first oracle-distinct verifier win (closes
 GAP-3-ties-vote; informs the DiffusionGemma gate). TIE-with-headroom ->
 honest null (GAP-3 frontier persists). No-headroom -> uninformative.

1 of 1 gate(s) failed; first failure: exp4209-oracle-distinct-arc-verifier-build.selector_trained (actual=False == expected=True)

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
